  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Translate the lesson into explicit state and permissive logic: A fault or stop request dominates start and leaves the motor in a safe stopped state.",
      "Inputs are simulator feedback (start_request, stop_request, fault_active); PLC logic owns motor_running, state_valid.",
      "Test the initial state, the valid condition, and at least one missing permissive.",
      "Current scene exposes five BOOL points only. It does not implement or display an enum state. No reference ladder is supplied; normal Run opens the editor until valid controller logic is loaded."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "Controller design guidance only; no executable reference controller is supplied. The motor graphic projects motor_running, not a measured motor feedback signal.",
      "steps": [
        "Require the documented inputs: start_request, stop_request, fault_active.",
        "Command the documented outputs: motor_running, state_valid.",
        "Remove PLC commands when the permissive is lost."
      ],
      "acceptance": "A fault or stop request dominates start and leaves the motor in a safe stopped state."
    },
    "assetRequirements": [],
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "Boolean inputs and motor/status outputs for an operating-state exercise. No enum-valued state or reference controller is supplied; author or load controller logic before Run.",
      "startConditions": [
        "Author or load a valid offline controller for the five declared BOOL points.",
        "Keep stop_request and fault_active false before applying start_request.",
        "The common watchdog tags are retained lesson metadata, not verified live PLC communication in this shell."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "Apply the requested input condition.",
        "Verify only the documented PLC outputs respond."
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "Controller logic must remove motor_running when a stop request or fault is active.",
        "Playback Stop freezes local motion; it does not write a PLC or implement the missing controller logic.",
        "Reset returns the module to its initial state."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "A missing or stale input must fail safe and remain diagnosable."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "When supplied controller logic commands motor_running, the shaft graphic and running indicator follow that output.",
        "The state-valid indicator follows state_valid; no named enum state is displayed.",
        "Fault/stop priority must be implemented and verified in the supplied controller logic."
      ]
    },
